/-!
# Reciprocal action and the SL₃ displacement orbit in 11.3.7(4)

The forward natural coordinates give the exact reciprocal common-axis index
and discharge the corank input of the existing normalization theorem. The
actual reciprocal representation retains the original selected conjugator.
In the SL₃ branch it is proved field-linear, and each nontrivial cyclic
commutator is recognized as a field line. Component transitivity constructs
the required x in N_G(V^g), with the left-conjugation convention x*g.
The published source assembly then applies; its original-line premise is
explicit in arbitrary multiplicity and is discharged in the one-copy case.

The Sp₄ recognition and the common-axis multiplicity/R₂ calculation remain
unfinished. These exports do not assert a completed proof of 11.3.7(4).
Source: Aschbacher--Smith, refs/quasithin.pdf, printed p.773.
-/
